 medals were awarded. The individual championship was won by Japan’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/12499"} "Takeichi, Baron Nishi"] ", who would later die on Iwo Jima during World War II."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The German riders did not attend for financial reasons, despite having several favored riders. The competitions had very small fields because of the travel distance to the American West Coast and the world-wide depression. The jumping competitions were restricted to men and military officers, as they would be through " [:a {:href "/editions/13/sports/EJP"} "1952"] ", with women first allowed to compete in Olympic jumping in " [:a {:href "/editions/48/sports/EJP"} "1956"] "."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/185097"} "Individual, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "14 August 1932"] "\n" [:td {} "11"] "\n" [:td {} "4"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/185098"} "Team, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "14 August 1932"] "\n" [:td {} "9"] "\n" [:td {} "3"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n11 (11/0)\n"] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n4 (4/0)\n"] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n\n\n" [:h2 {} "Medals"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {:colspan "2"} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] "\n" [:th {:colspan "2"} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] "\n" [:th {:colspan "2"} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {:class "top"} [:a {:href "/results/185097"} "Individual, Men"]] "\n" [:td {:style "vertical-align: top"} [:a {:href "/athletes/12499"} "Takeichi, Baron Nishi"]] [:td {:style "vertical-align: top"} [:a {:href "/countries/JP